= Hello, Mosaic

This file is a placeholder so the project layout is exercisable
once the parser lands in MVP 0. See `manifest.md` §2 for the syntax
this is sketching toward.

The renderer now supports PDF WinAnsi text plus every
Unicode-addressable glyph the Adobe Core 14 Latin fonts ship
beyond WinAnsi, via per-document /Differences encodings: café
culture, §1 legal citations, German Straße addresses, ¶ pilcrows,
© copyright marks, curly "smart" quotes, Polish Łódź, Czech
Příliš žluťoučký kůň, Hungarian árvíztűrő, Romanian mâine. Math
operators (≤ ≥ ≠ √ ∂ ∑ −) and the fi/fl ligatures round out the
set. 314 of the 315 glyphs each Latin AFM carries are reachable;
the lone holdout is `commaaccent`, a spacing diacritic with no
Unicode codepoint that exists only as a metric reference for
the compound comma-below forms. Scripts without Core 14 glyphs
(Cyrillic, CJK, Greek) still substitute with `?` and warn until
full font embedding lands (issue #9).
